# Mobile release policy tests must move with the versions

If you edit `PLAYSPACE_RELEASE_POLICY` or `YEE_RELEASE_POLICY` (`latest_version`, `minimum_supported_version`, `latest_build`, `minimum_supported_build`), update the contract tests in the same change.

- Playspace / COPA → `tests/products/playspace/test_api_endpoints.py` (`test_playspace_mobile_release_policy_is_public`)
- YEE → `tests/products/yee/test_mobile_release_policy.py` (`test_yee_mobile_release_policy_is_public`)

Keep those assertions as explicit version strings. Do not import the policy constants to avoid a test edit.

Do not retarget synthetic fixture versions in `tests/products/test_mobile_release_policy_sources.py` or the mobile apps' `release-policy` unit tests unless the resolver/evaluator behavior itself changed.

Full procedure: skill `mobile-release-policy-test-sync`.
